repository-code: https://github.com/KatherLab/SwarmMed
url: https://github.com/KatherLab/SwarmMed
abstract: >-
  SwarmMed is an open-source platform for running decentralized (swarm) learning
  studies on biomedical data across institutions. It provides a web interface
  (SwarmMedHub) and a command-line interface (SwarmMedCLI) over the NVIDIA FLARE
  client-controlled swarm workflow, covering project and consortium setup,
  network provisioning and startup-kit distribution, site-local data registration
  and sandboxed validation, decentralized training, and results synthesis. Sites
  exchange model parameters and training metadata; no message sent by SwarmMed
  or NVIDIA FLARE contains raw data.
keywords:
  - swarm learning
  - federated learning
  - decentralized learning
  - privacy-preserving machine learning
  - medical imaging
  - biomedical data analysis
